WEBVTT

00:00.020 --> 00:29.971
The Old Man and the Big Tree

00:00.547 --> 00:02.293
It's the fantasy between
an old man and a big tree.

00:02.420 --> 00:04.840
The big tree that has lived for a long time.

00:04.940 --> 00:08.047
uses its last remaining energy
to give the old man a miracle.

00:08.986 --> 00:09.620
Hey!

00:10.646 --> 00:12.173
What are you trying to do to this tree?

00:12.260 --> 00:13.767
Of course, that zekova tree will also be...

00:14.080 --> 00:16.295
No! Please don't cut it down!

00:16.514 --> 00:17.501
We'll squat around it.

00:17.608 --> 00:19.459
I will protect him!

00:20.112 --> 00:21.812
Come back, old man!

00:21.992 --> 00:26.457
Perhaps both you and I have lived too long.

00:26.644 --> 00:29.831
Black Jack, Today's Karte - The Old Man and the Big Tree.

00:30.075 --> 00:36.698
I'm going to fly to where you are.

00:30.075 --> 00:36.698
kimi no moto e tonde yuku yo

00:37.033 --> 00:44.039
I know I can spread my wings when I want to see you.

00:37.033 --> 00:44.039
aitai toki tsubasa hiraku

00:44.624 --> 00:47.709
Nobody knows

00:44.624 --> 00:47.709
dara nimo wakaranai

00:48.128 --> 00:51.547
when a miracle might occur,

00:48.128 --> 00:51.547
kiseki wa itsu okiru?

00:51.548 --> 00:57.970
but it feels like my wish is finally coming true.

00:51.548 --> 00:57.970
nozomi wa kanaeraresou de

00:57.971 --> 01:04.768
Because there's only one place I want to go,

00:57.971 --> 01:04.768
mukau basho wa hitotsu shika nai kara

01:04.769 --> 01:08.021
iro asenai omoi yosete

01:04.769 --> 01:08.021
I gather my feelings whose colors never fade,

01:08.022 --> 01:11.567
and now it seems I'm dreaming.

01:08.022 --> 01:11.567
saa Dreaming now

01:12.152 --> 01:15.487
I'm living for your sake?

01:12.152 --> 01:15.487
kimi no tame ni iketeru

01:15.488 --> 01:18.657
I will be your strength,

01:15.488 --> 01:18.657
donna chikara nimo naru

01:18.950 --> 01:21.869
no matter how far apart we are.

01:18.950 --> 01:21.869
Far away Far away harukana

01:21.870 --> 01:25.664
So Freedom. So Freedom.

01:25.790 --> 01:29.251
I will send you

01:25.790 --> 01:29.251
kimi no tame no okurou

01:29.252 --> 01:32.504
the beautiful blossom of this flower.

01:29.252 --> 01:32.504
kirei ni saita hana wo

01:32.672 --> 01:35.591
So let's look for shooting stars.

01:32.672 --> 01:35.591
Shooting Star Shooting Star sagasou

01:35.592 --> 01:39.595
So Freedom. So Freedom.

02:13.940 --> 02:15.882
You're alone here, Master?

02:15.882 --> 02:20.633
Kumi-chan went out with Pinoco-chan and the others.

02:20.968 --> 02:22.611
You take such good care of her.

02:23.097 --> 02:26.683
She said they were going to the park in the next town.

02:27.518 --> 02:28.554
The next town?

02:28.853 --> 02:30.979
The park with a big zelkova tree?

02:31.257 --> 02:32.491
You know .about that?

02:32.732 --> 02:34.728
Yeah, I saw it once before.

02:36.361 --> 02:38.570
<i>I wonder if that old man man is still there,</i>

02:39.447 --> 02:41.133
<i>standing by that big zelkova tree.</i>

02:48.206 --> 02:51.416
Originally "The Old Man and the Tree" by Tezuka Osamu

02:48.206 --> 02:51.416
The Old Man and the Big Tree

03:00.165 --> 03:05.419
It's Pinoco's joyous forest adventure...

03:05.837 --> 03:07.939
Parks are so relaxing.

03:08.423 --> 03:09.548
Yeah.

03:09.549 --> 03:14.386
I didn't know there was such a
green place so close to home.

03:14.387 --> 03:17.848
I can't wait for lunch!

03:24.562 --> 03:26.232
Hey!

03:27.734 --> 03:29.109
You darned dog!

03:29.110 --> 03:30.736
What are you trying to do to this tree?!

03:34.182 --> 03:36.200
What was that for?!

03:36.201 --> 03:38.953
That's my line exactly!

03:40.080 --> 03:42.915
Excuse us, but did Largo try to do something wrong?

03:42.916 --> 03:44.959
Heck yes, she did!

03:44.960 --> 03:48.185
What did that dog just try to do?!

03:53.343 --> 03:57.137
Are you the owner of this tree?

03:57.597 --> 03:59.306
I don't own it.

03:59.307 --> 04:05.062
But I've been looking after this tree for forty long years.

04:05.375 --> 04:07.691
So you love this tree.

04:07.691 --> 04:09.066
Yes, I do.

04:09.067 --> 04:12.361
This tree saved my life after all.

04:12.494 --> 04:14.363
It saved your life?

04:14.823 --> 04:16.323
Wanna hear about it?

04:16.324 --> 04:17.519
Yeah.

04:18.076 --> 04:19.118
All right!

04:19.119 --> 04:21.495
There!

04:22.163 --> 04:25.624
Yeah? Then I'll tell you.

04:26.835 --> 04:29.420
It was during the war.

04:33.925 --> 04:38.053
I was still a kid then, and I had just
been separated from my family.

04:38.054 --> 04:40.235
I didn't know what to do.

04:40.598 --> 04:42.683
We were surrounded by flames.

04:42.684 --> 04:46.043
I ran all over, but every place I went was burning.

04:46.354 --> 04:51.525
Just when I thought nowhere was
safe and I was about to give up,

04:58.241 --> 05:01.709
I found this zelkova tree.

05:07.584 --> 05:13.142
I somehow reached this tree and
spent the long night under it.

05:34.069 --> 05:36.362
It was a mysterious scene.

05:36.363 --> 05:39.114
Nothing was left as far as I could see,

05:39.115 --> 05:43.545
but for some reason there wasn't
even a single burn on this tree.

05:48.166 --> 05:55.421
Its big trunk and strong roots protected me.

05:56.132 --> 06:00.427
That's how he saved my life.

06:02.677 --> 06:04.973
That's a mysterious story.

06:04.974 --> 06:08.681
My life's been with this tree ever since then.

06:09.229 --> 06:14.066
I became the manager of this park,
just so I could spend time with this tree.

06:17.070 --> 06:20.656
If I found worms, I got rid of them.

06:22.951 --> 06:26.286
If he didn't look well, I gave him fertilizer.

06:26.546 --> 06:29.012
When he caught a disease,
I cared for him without any sleep.

06:30.765 --> 06:35.087
Over the years, the tree became very dear to me.

06:35.088 --> 06:39.738
I know he's far older than me, but it feels like he's my son.

06:40.093 --> 06:42.010
Your son...

06:42.011 --> 06:44.721
He's older and you're younger, but he's your son?

06:44.926 --> 06:46.640
I don't have any family.

06:46.641 --> 06:50.436
I think I was able to live for so long because of him.

06:50.658 --> 06:55.008
Now I understand why you care for the tree so much.

06:55.275 --> 06:57.899
Yes, that's a wonderful story.

06:59.028 --> 07:02.016
So Largo almost made a huge boo-boo.

07:07.120 --> 07:10.873
Somehow, this tree looks a bit troubled.

07:15.795 --> 07:17.629
Do you want us to arrange that?

07:17.630 --> 07:19.882
Yes, I'd appreciate that.

07:21.885 --> 07:23.385
Here it is.

07:23.386 --> 07:25.220
Who the heck are you?!

07:25.221 --> 07:27.097
We're from city hall.

07:27.098 --> 07:29.808
What are people from city hall doing here?

07:29.809 --> 07:32.728
This park will be remodeled soon.

07:32.729 --> 07:34.771
We came to check the place.

07:34.772 --> 07:36.482
Remodeled?

07:36.483 --> 07:38.942
No one told me about that!

07:38.943 --> 07:40.991
Then what about this tree?

07:41.404 --> 07:44.352
This area will become an athletic field..

07:44.782 --> 07:48.035
Of course, that zelkova tree will also be cut down.

07:48.036 --> 07:51.246
Bull! I won't let you cut this tree down!

07:51.247 --> 07:52.831
Make it stop now!

07:53.333 --> 07:55.375
But you know...

07:55.376 --> 07:57.632
It's already been made official.

07:57.705 --> 07:59.482
We can't overturn the decision.

07:59.506 --> 08:01.924
The area residents have already agreed to this as well.

08:01.925 --> 08:05.010
No! Please don't cut it down!

08:05.011 --> 08:08.639
Sir, it's already happening.

08:08.929 --> 08:11.642
We will be cutting it down in a week.

08:11.643 --> 08:13.727
The decision is official already.

08:22.362 --> 08:24.488
Please cheer up, sir.

08:26.157 --> 08:30.452
How can he when the tree he's been caring
for like a son will be cut.down?

08:30.954 --> 08:32.496
That's it?

08:32.497 --> 08:33.664
You're giving up just like that?

08:34.931 --> 08:36.291
It's such a great tree.

08:36.292 --> 08:39.294
There must be a way to stop from cutting it down.

08:39.295 --> 08:41.004
But how?

08:41.005 --> 08:43.465
We'll start with direct negotiations at City Hall.

08:48.304 --> 08:49.680
I see.

08:49.681 --> 08:52.140
I understand your point.

08:52.141 --> 08:53.809
T-Then...

08:54.185 --> 08:58.188
Unfortunately, we cannot fulfill your request.

08:58.507 --> 08:59.458
Why?

08:59.482 --> 09:01.775
That's the way government works.

09:01.776 --> 09:08.490
We cannot stop a project we have been working
on for so long for just one old man.

09:08.741 --> 09:12.578
Then we just need to prove that the tree is valuable, right?

09:13.327 --> 09:16.039
Well, maybe.

09:20.920 --> 09:23.631
What's the matter?

09:24.257 --> 09:27.050
I know how to save tree!

09:28.815 --> 09:29.815
How?

09:30.263 --> 09:32.928
We can have the tree certified as a precious tree!

09:33.195 --> 09:34.195
Certified?

09:35.685 --> 09:36.977
Some well-known precious trees we know include

09:37.118 --> 09:39.118
Jomon Sugi on Yakushima Island

09:39.214 --> 09:41.856
and Usuzumi Zakura in Neo-Mura Village.

09:42.317 --> 09:45.444
They might not carry as much weight as national
monuments or World Heritage sites,

09:45.445 --> 09:50.115
but, if it's approved as a precious tree,
we should be able to prevent it from being cut down!

09:50.116 --> 09:52.784
I see! That's a plan!

09:52.785 --> 09:56.232
But who decides whether it's a precious tree?

10:05.673 --> 10:07.257
A tree doctor?

10:07.258 --> 10:10.552
There sure are many unique occupations in the world.

10:10.553 --> 10:15.974
Everyone. Unfortunately, this tree can't
be certified as a precious tree.

10:15.975 --> 10:17.809
W-Why not?!

10:17.810 --> 10:22.022
It's a zelkova that has been watching
over this town for such a long time!

10:22.305 --> 10:24.066
It's half-dead.

10:24.067 --> 10:27.486
Even if it stays here, it'll only last for a few years at best.

10:28.406 --> 10:29.839
No way!

10:30.172 --> 10:32.159
Then cure it!

10:32.698 --> 10:34.242
That's not possible.

10:34.452 --> 10:37.287
It's dying of old age.

10:37.584 --> 10:39.492
Can we transfer it somewhere?

10:39.672 --> 10:41.625
If we can move it elsewhere...

10:41.824 --> 10:44.711
As I mentioned, it's dying.

10:44.712 --> 10:48.840
Even if we move it, I don't know if its roots will settle.

10:49.087 --> 10:51.802
I believe there's nothing we can do.

10:56.766 --> 10:58.141
Listen here.

10:58.142 --> 11:01.269
We still have a week, so don't give up hope.

11:01.394 --> 11:02.646
Yeah.

11:02.647 --> 11:04.369
You should cheer up too.

11:04.691 --> 11:06.929
Thank you all.

11:07.360 --> 11:10.862
You're right. We should fight to the end.

11:10.863 --> 11:12.406
That's right!

11:12.407 --> 11:15.343
We'll protect this tree!

11:15.873 --> 11:17.369
Let's do it!

11:17.370 --> 11:18.635
Yeah!

11:29.674 --> 11:31.174
What are you doing?

11:31.423 --> 11:34.386
We're protecting the old man's zelkova tree.

11:34.387 --> 11:35.580
Zelkova tree?

11:35.847 --> 11:37.301
What about that tree?

11:37.465 --> 11:39.745
Sign: "Protect This Tree"

11:37.515 --> 11:39.850
The city is cutting it down for an athletic field.

11:39.851 --> 11:43.812
The tree is half-dead, and the
tree doctor won't help either.

11:44.480 --> 11:47.452
I didn't understand the whole thing,
but I guess it's being cut down?

11:47.650 --> 11:49.090
That's right.

11:49.485 --> 11:52.362
Then that old man must be bummed out right about now.

11:52.474 --> 11:54.948
Do you know that man?

11:54.996 --> 11:55.556
Yeah.

11:56.534 --> 11:59.870
He preached to me when I drove by that tree.

12:00.955 --> 12:03.667
He said that the exhaust from the
car would damage the tree.

12:05.877 --> 12:09.921
<i>But, if that zelkova is taken from that man...</i>

12:12.467 --> 12:15.427
How can I give up?

12:15.253 --> 12:17.813
Don't Cut This Tree!

12:15.253 --> 12:17.813
Save the Zelkova!!

12:16.040 --> 12:17.793
I'll protect him,

12:17.889 --> 12:20.015
no matter what it takes.

12:37.408 --> 12:39.324
Please read this!

12:39.351 --> 12:41.224
Don't Cut This Tree!!

12:56.135 --> 13:00.764
The tree is to be cut down tomorrow,
but there is still something we can do.

13:00.924 --> 13:01.977
Like what?

13:02.171 --> 13:03.524
What can we do?

13:03.768 --> 13:06.269
I don't know what it is, but I'll do it.

13:06.498 --> 13:07.331
I know.

13:07.355 --> 13:09.409
This is our last resort.

13:09.824 --> 13:11.691
So what are we doing?

13:14.111 --> 13:17.030
We'll squat around it.

13:17.384 --> 13:19.699
They won't be able to approach it if we do that.

13:19.700 --> 13:21.535
Let's do it!

13:21.536 --> 13:25.330
It'll be for the long haul, but there's no other way.

13:25.331 --> 13:27.127
That's enough.

13:29.001 --> 13:33.380
Thank you for going along with this old man's dream,

13:33.756 --> 13:35.882
but it's all enough now.

13:36.801 --> 13:38.677
What's enough?

13:38.678 --> 13:40.220
It's not at all!

13:40.221 --> 13:41.513
Yeah!

13:41.514 --> 13:43.557
We've come this far!

13:43.558 --> 13:44.724
It's OK.

13:44.725 --> 13:49.229
There's no one else who will suffer from losing this tree,

13:49.230 --> 13:51.231
and he's dying too.

13:51.418 --> 13:54.192
His days are numbered even if he stays here.

13:54.986 --> 13:56.266
So really, that's enough.

13:56.487 --> 13:59.353
Thank you so much for what you've done.

14:15.631 --> 14:16.989
Drink!

14:18.509 --> 14:19.950
There!

14:23.264 --> 14:26.558
This will be my last night with you.

14:26.559 --> 14:30.937
We've been watching over this town for a long time.

14:31.772 --> 14:33.017
Yes, for a long time.

14:48.706 --> 14:50.874
W-What was that?

14:50.875 --> 14:51.906
A vision?

14:54.128 --> 14:59.898
Perhaps you and I have lived too long.

15:08.726 --> 15:11.638
Sheesh! Really!

15:12.146 --> 15:14.114
Pinoco? What is it now?

15:14.273 --> 15:17.442
Doc! Listen to this!

15:17.443 --> 15:19.235
I've had it this time.

15:22.038 --> 15:23.198
What?

15:23.199 --> 15:25.367
See? Isn't it terrible?

15:31.207 --> 15:34.292
Maybe that man's trying to die with the tree.

15:35.169 --> 15:36.544
Let's hurry to the zelkova!

15:41.133 --> 15:42.968
Now the booze is gone too.

15:48.307 --> 15:50.308
I should get going.

15:52.228 --> 15:56.773
Zelkova tree, I'll be going first.

16:17.612 --> 16:18.612
It's him!

16:19.338 --> 16:20.430
We're too late!

16:22.508 --> 16:24.217
Come back, old man!

16:24.218 --> 16:25.680
Come on!

16:26.053 --> 16:27.053
He's still alive.

16:27.054 --> 16:28.346
Let's rush him home.

16:28.347 --> 16:29.681
Aye-aye!

16:41.508 --> 16:42.713
It's an emergency operation.

16:42.737 --> 16:44.446
Pinoco, this is a critical one.

16:44.447 --> 16:45.245
Yes.

16:46.365 --> 16:47.405
Commencing the operation.

16:53.581 --> 16:58.043
Doc, even if he survives, maybe he'll—

16:58.044 --> 16:59.448
Cut the chit-chat.

16:59.901 --> 17:00.914
We're in the middle of a procedure.

17:03.174 --> 17:04.814
It's lucky he fell the way he did.

17:05.134 --> 17:07.362
Otherwise, he could have died instantly.

17:10.222 --> 17:11.343
Suturing the incision.

17:11.724 --> 17:13.975
Pinoco, prepare the respirator.

17:13.976 --> 17:15.075
OK!

17:22.031 --> 17:22.464
No!

17:23.116 --> 17:24.077
I'm going to shock him.

17:27.490 --> 17:29.449
Come back, old man!

17:29.631 --> 17:30.642
Old man!

17:38.167 --> 17:39.626
Is this...

17:42.546 --> 17:44.887
T-This is that fateful day.

17:45.841 --> 17:47.171
It's a dream.

17:47.426 --> 17:50.261
It's the perfect last dream for me.

17:51.138 --> 17:55.306
I was supposed to die on this day.

18:02.358 --> 18:08.196
I'm such a lucky man to be able to
see you until the end of my life.

18:08.906 --> 18:12.033
Are you telling me to come there?

18:17.164 --> 18:18.957
Now what, Zelkova?

18:18.958 --> 18:21.988
Do you still need to tell me something?

18:40.604 --> 18:42.772
A-Are you...

18:55.063 --> 18:57.959
M-My thoughts came through?

18:58.372 --> 19:01.374
So you knew how I felt!

19:16.056 --> 19:17.198
He'll survive.

19:17.641 --> 19:18.933
What a man he is.

19:48.380 --> 19:50.924
I guess I failed to die.

19:51.884 --> 19:53.927
Sir, um...

19:54.511 --> 19:55.887
The mountain pass to the west...

19:57.014 --> 20:00.391
Can you take me to the mountain pass to the west?

20:00.935 --> 20:01.957
That...

20:12.891 --> 20:13.696
There!

20:13.747 --> 20:14.654
That's it!

20:18.714 --> 20:19.786
Is that...

20:19.787 --> 20:21.388
A zelkova tree?

20:25.834 --> 20:26.751
H-Here!

20:26.752 --> 20:29.712
I'll walk on my own.

20:43.894 --> 20:45.228
This is it!

20:45.229 --> 20:47.563
See? There's a white scar right here!

20:47.940 --> 20:50.740
Is there something special about this zelkova tree?

20:51.130 --> 20:53.528
I died once.

20:56.148 --> 20:59.806
And that's when I met that zelkova tree.

21:00.119 --> 21:02.802
The zelkova told me,

21:03.163 --> 21:08.835
"There's a zelkova from the seed I spread
on the western mountain pass,

21:08.836 --> 21:14.048
so take care of it like you did me."

21:20.764 --> 21:22.557
I was so happy.

21:22.558 --> 21:25.184
That was the first time I could talk with him.

21:25.185 --> 21:29.689
I promised him that I'd take good care of it.

21:30.774 --> 21:33.622
Then what do you think he said?

21:34.319 --> 21:36.404
He said, "Thank you."

21:41.702 --> 21:43.619
That's a mysterious story.

21:43.620 --> 21:46.414
Do you think the zelkova really said that?

21:46.656 --> 21:48.791
I couldn't care less.

21:48.792 --> 21:51.794
The tree branch saved him from the fall,

21:51.795 --> 21:54.213
and the tree cheered him up in his dream.

21:57.593 --> 22:00.595
Either way, the tree saved him.

22:01.930 --> 22:03.806
You don't believe his story?

22:05.184 --> 22:07.095
The old man found a reason to live.

22:07.478 --> 22:08.811
That's good enough for me.

22:24.097 --> 22:29.209
As you look at the ground uncertainly,

22:24.097 --> 22:29.209
tamerai gachi no fuseta hitomi

22:29.210 --> 22:34.506
I gently pull your hair closer to me.

22:29.210 --> 22:34.506
kono te ga sono kami hikiyoseteta

22:35.137 --> 22:41.638
You didn't speak, but only sighed,

22:35.137 --> 22:41.638
nani mo iezu ni kobore ochita tameiki

22:41.639 --> 22:46.101
and wet my chest with your tears.

22:41.639 --> 22:46.101
namida ga mune wo nurashita

22:46.102 --> 22:51.356
You longed to hear it, even if it was a lie.

22:46.102 --> 22:51.356
use demo ii... to kitto nozonde ita

22:51.357 --> 22:56.111
But I couldn't give you the answer you wanted.

22:51.357 --> 22:56.111
kimi no kimochi ni kotae kirezu

22:56.112 --> 23:04.536
If I gave you that answer, despite my cowardice,

22:56.112 --> 23:04.536
okubyou na boku ga moshi sono toki kotaetetara mada

23:04.537 --> 23:08.123
would we still be together?

23:04.537 --> 23:08.123
tsuzuiteita noka?

23:08.124 --> 23:13.420
That irregular breath my body was accustomed to,

23:08.124 --> 23:13.420
karada ga oboeta fukisoku na breath

23:13.424 --> 23:18.884
I want to feel it one more time.

23:13.424 --> 23:18.884
mou ichido subete de kanjitai

23:18.885 --> 23:24.389
The breath of surprise when I lost everything.

23:18.885 --> 23:24.389
subete wo nakushita fuyoui na breath

23:24.390 --> 23:33.565
And the pain that binds me every time I feel regret.

23:24.390 --> 23:33.565
kuyamu tabi mata sono itami ga shimetsukeru

23:45.078 --> 24:15.035
Black Queen

23:45.538 --> 23:47.071
A female Black Jack makes her appearance.

23:47.365 --> 23:49.666
She's beautiful, cold-hearted,
and a queen of the scalpel.

23:49.705 --> 23:51.898
People call her "Black Queen".

23:52.305 --> 23:53.651
We have a seriously injured patient!

23:53.738 --> 23:55.751
All right, prepare for an amputation.

23:55.818 --> 23:58.571
He was planning to go
abroad to play soccer!

23:58.786 --> 24:01.053
The decision is best made quickly.

24:01.173 --> 24:03.446
His mother was very sad about it.

24:03.473 --> 24:04.480
Will you marry me?

24:04.633 --> 24:05.633
It's suspicious.

24:06.554 --> 24:09.100
You want me to choose between
you and my job?

24:09.521 --> 24:11.082
Do you want your boyfriend to die?!

24:11.355 --> 24:14.475
Black Jack, Next Karte - Black Queen.

24:15.984 --> 24:17.776
Karte NG...
